Here is the commit message:
tcp: Fix data-races around sysctl_tcp_migrate_req.

While reading sysctl_tcp_migrate_req, it can be changed concurrently.
Thus, we need to add READ_ONCE() to its readers.

Fixes: f9ac779f881c ("net: Introduce net.ipv4.tcp_migrate_req.")
Signed-off-by: Kuniyuki Iwashima <kuniyu@amazon.com>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>

Here is the root cause:
The bug is caused by concurrent modifications to the `sysctl_tcp_migrate_req` variable while it is being read, leading to potential data races. This can result in inconsistent or unexpected behavior when the value is accessed by multiple threads without proper synchronization.

Here is the patch:

